I'll re-review only the round-1 timestamp fix: whether `rows()` still normalizes on read, and whether the writer, test, and docs stay consistent.The round-1 finding is resolved. `Restorer::rows()` replaces `panel_state.updated_at` with `Dataset::CLOCK` only when `$wallClock` is true, and that argument defaults to false. `Writer::write()` is the only caller that passes `wallClock: true`. `PopulatedDatabaseTest` reads with the default, so a stored timestamp that differs from the dump fails the `toBe` comparison.

The writer header matches the `normalisation` string in every dump and still describes that capture path. The `Restorer` docblock and `README.md` both state that a restored database is read as stored.

